    "id": "10.12688/wellcomeopenres.28205.1",
    "title": "The genome sequence of the Pheasant Shell, Tricolia pullus (Linnaeus, 1758) (Trochida: Phasianellidae)",
    "abstract": "We present a genome assembly from an individual  Tricolia pullus (Pheasant Shell; Mollusca; Gastropoda; Trochida; Phasianellidae). The primary assembly has a total length of 769.49 megabases. Most of the primary assembly (99.07%) is scaffolded into 8 chromosomal pseudomolecules. The mitochondrial genome has also been assembled, with a length of 18.23 kilobases. Gene annotation of the primary assembly by Ensembl identified 18,405 protein-coding genes. This assembly was generated as part of the Darwin Tree of Life project, which produces genomes for eukaryotic species found in Britain and Ireland.",
