    "id": "10.21203/rs.3.rs-11333020/v1",
    "title": "A SHAP-Guided Retrieval-Augmented Generation Framework for Predictive Maintenance Decision Support",
    "abstract": "Abstract  Predictive maintenance models can reach high detection performance, but their outputs often remain difficult to operationalize in industrial environments, where maintenance decisions require interpretability and actionable guidance. Existing approaches rarely establish a direct link between failure predictions, model explanations, and maintenance-oriented recommendations. This study proposes a proof-of-concept framework that extends retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) to tabular predictive maintenance data through SHAP-guided query construction. A supervised machine learning model is trained to predict machine failures from operational data. SHAP explanations are then extracted to identify the dominant factors driving each prediction and converted into structured queries. These queries guide retrieval from an experimental maintenance knowledge base using embedding-based similarity search. The retrieved information is used by a generation module to produce case-specific maintenance recommendations aligned with the predictive output and its explanation. The framework is evaluated on a benchmark predictive maintenance dataset, where the predictive model shows strong failure detection capability, with particular improvement in recall for rare failure events. The retrieval module further indicates that explanation-derived queries can retrieve semantically relevant maintenance information. The results support the feasibility of integrating predictive modeling, SHAP-based explanation, retrieval, and LLM-based generation for maintenance-oriented interpretation. The proposed framework remains a proof of concept and does not yet constitute a fully validated industrial decision-support system.",
