    "id": "10.64898/2026.10.24.761506",
    "title": "OTTER: Orchestrated Transcriptomic, Tumor-xenograft (PDX/CDX), and Epigenomic Reporting Workflow",
    "abstract": "Summary  Tumor xenograft sequencing libraries inevitably contain infiltrating murine host reads, but conventional deconvolution tools fail on bisulfite sequencing (BS-seq) because chemical C-to-T deamination collapses sequence entropy and destroys graft recall (  Availability and implementation  OTTER is implemented in Go and Rust, runs on x86 64 Linux (including CentOS 7 with glibc 2.17), and is freely available open-source under the MIT License at  https://github.com/otterlab-bio/otter ; test and validation data are provided at  https://huggingface.co/datasets/fallingstar10/otter-data .  Contact  xx-wang119@hotmail.com ,  fzhang@cmpt.ac.cn Supplementary information  Supplementary data are available with this preprint.",
